<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Visigothic Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">418 CE – 721 CE · capital Toulouse</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Gothic kingdom first at Toulouse, then at Toledo, that ruled Iberia for two centuries until the Muslim conquest of 711.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After sacking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 410 under Alaric, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> moved into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. In 418 Rome settled them as federates in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-aquitaine">Aquitaine</a>, with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/county-of-toulouse">Toulouse</a> as their capital, under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wallia">Wallia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-i">Theodoric I</a> died fighting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-catalaunian-plains">Catalaunian Plains</a> in 451, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euric">Euric</a> made the kingdom fully independent and expanded deep into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Gothic warriors ruled a mostly Roman population, at first under separate laws. The kings were Arian until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reccared-i">Reccared</a> converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a> in 589, after which the Councils of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a> became central to government. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liuvigild">Leovigild</a> conquered the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-the-suebi">Kingdom of the Suebi</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/recceswinth">Recceswinth</a> issued the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigothic-code">Visigothic Code</a> in 654.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i">Clovis</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaric-ii">Alaric II</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-vouille">Vouillé</a> in 507, and the centre of the kingdom shifted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a> became the capital by the 560s. In 711 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tariq-ibn-ziyad">Tariq ibn Ziyad</a> defeated King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roderic">Roderic</a>, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>; the last Visigothic outpost in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/septimania">Septimania</a> fell around 720. The Christian kingdoms of the north claimed Visigothic descent.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/visigothic-kingdom.jpg" alt="Visigothic Kingdom" width="320" height="309"><figcaption>Image: You may select the license of your choice. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leovigild_CNG_97-722237_(obverse).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>418 CE – 721 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Toulouse</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Euric, Leovigild, Reccared</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Arian, then Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Latin, Gothic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>, <a href="/countries/portugal">Portugal</a>, <a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of the Visigoths, Kingdom of Toulouse, Kingdom of Toledo</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=570&amp;focus=visigothic-kingdom" aria-label="Visigothic Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4715 632 640 512" role=